<!--
    mapGlobals: a global read wider than the Symbol at its address.

    Ported from decompiler/cpp/funcdata_varnode.cc (Funcdata::mapGlobals,
    coverVarnodes) and printc.cc (PrintC::pushMismatchSymbol). When the
    persistent Varnodes at an address run past the end of the global Symbol
    there, upstream warns, names each uncovered interior Varnode after the
    Symbol (`small_4`), and prints the wide read as `_small`. kuna's
    ActionMapGlobals did nothing, so the wide read printed as the Symbol
    itself or as `dat_200000`, and no warning was given.

    Authored x86-64 (nasm): g adds the 8-byte value at 0x200000 to the
    zero-extended 4-byte value at 0x200004; `small` is mapped as an int4 at
    0x200000.

    Before: `return small + (uint8)dat_200004;` with no warning.
    Fixed: `return _small + (uint8)small_4;` with the overlap warning.

-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
48a100002000000000008b0c25040020004801c8c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="g"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>map address r0x200000 int4 small</com>
  <com>lo fu g</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="MAPGLOBALS #1: the overlap warning is given" min="1" max="1">Globals starting with '_' overlap smaller symbols at the same address</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="MAPGLOBALS #2: the wide read is the Symbol with a leading underscore" min="1" max="1">return _small \+</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="MAPGLOBALS #3: the uncovered upper half is named after the Symbol" min="1" max="1">\(uint8\)small_4;</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
